{"vid": [{"id": "vid", "headword": "विद्", "headword_slp1": "vid", "fold": "vid", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "1 विद् वेत्ति (वेद), pp. विदित॑ or वित्त (q.v.) know,\nunderstand, learn, perceive, experience, feel;\n think or be mindful of\n(acc. or gen.), know how to (infin.);\n believe, suppose, know or\nrecognize as, declare to be, take for, call, name (2 acc. or acc. & nom.\nw. इति). C. वेद॑यते, ˚ति make known, announce, report;\n inform of,\nteach (2 acc.);\n take for, learn or know — to be (2 acc.);\n perceive,\nnotice, experience, feel. D. विविदिषति wish to know, inquire after\n(acc.). — अनु know thoroughly (lit. along). आ know well or exactly.\nC. address, invite, announce, proclaim, prescribe, inform;\n offer,\npresent. नि C. cause to know, announce, report, communicate to (dat.,\ngen., or loc.);\n name, call (2 acc.), offer, present, surrender\n(आत्मानम् refl.). विनि & संनि C. make known, announce, report,\noffer, present, surrender. परि know very well. प्र know. C. make\nknown, announce, relate. प्रति understand, know. C. make known,\nannounce, tell;\n acquaint with (2 acc.);\n offer, entrust, commit. वि\ndiscern, know. सम् know or understand (together);\n consent, agree. C.\ncause to know, inform, instruct;\n make known, communicate.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2 विद् (mostly —˚) knowing.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "3 विद् विन्द॑ति विन्द॑˚ते (वित्ते॑), pp. वित्त॑ & विन्न\n(q.v.) find, meet with, get, obtain;\n visit, befall;\n have, possess;\n find\nout for, procure (dat.);\n look for, turn to (acc.);\n M. (A.) take to wife\n(±भार्याम्), find a husband, marry;\n bring forth (±सुतम्). P.M. be\nfound, be there (impers.), exist. विद्य॑ते (˚ति) there is (esp. w.\nन), य॑था विदे॑ as it is, i.e. as usual or as well as possible. D.\nविवित्सति wish to find. I. वे॑विदत्, वे॑विदान be present. — अधि\nsupersede, supplant. अनु find (after), get, obtain, take hold of;\n M.\nभार्याम् take to wife. P. be found, exist. अभि find, find out, know.\nआ get hold of, get at, acquire, incur, undergo. P. be, exist. निस्\ndivide from (abl.);\n M. get rid of (gen.), take off (acc.);\n P. become\ndepressed or dispirited, get weary of or disgusted with (abl., instr.,\nr. acc.). परि P. be married with the younger brother before the elder\nhas married. सम् M. find, get hold of, acquire, win. P. be found, be\nthere (esp. w. न), exist, belong to (gen.). — Cf. अधिविन्न,\nअ॑नुवित्त, निर्विण, परिवित्त, परिविन्न, विदान, संविदान॑.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "4 विद् (—˚) finding, winning, procuring.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "vida": [{"id": "vida", "headword": "विद", "headword_slp1": "vida", "fold": "vida", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "विद (—˚) = 2 विद्.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["विदः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vidaH"]}], "vidagDa": [{"id": "vidagDa", "headword": "विदग्ध", "headword_slp1": "vidagDa", "fold": "vidagDa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "विदग्ध a. burnt, inflamed;\n burnt i.e. taught by\nexperience, knowing, witty, cunning, clever.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["विदग्धः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vidagDaH"]}], "vidagDacuqamaRi": [{"id": "vidagDacUqAmaRi", "headword": "विदग्धचूडामणि", "headword_slp1": "vidagDacUqAmaRi", "fold": "vidagDacuqamaRi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "विदग्धचूडामणि m. N. of a parrot (the\ncrest-jewel of the wise).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "vidagData": [{"id": "vidagDatA", "headword": "विदग्धता", "headword_slp1": "vidagDatA", "fold": "vidagData", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "विदग्धता f. cleverness, skill in (loc.).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "vidatra": [{"id": "vidatra", "headword": "विदत्र", "headword_slp1": "vidatra", "fold": "vidatra", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ca